# AI_Systems — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Games needing shared AI architecture (strategy_simulation; action games with complex AI).

## 2. This document owns
- AI architecture: perception stack, decision layers (utility/behavior tree/state machine), navigation approach.
- Shared AI archetypes (IDs, trigger conditions, parameter meanings) reusable across enemies/units.
- Performance budgets for agent counts and tick policies.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- What each enemy wants (design intent) — Enemy_Design.
- Unit roster and stats — Unit_Design.
- Boss staging — Encounter_Design.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Architecture overview / 2. Perception / 3. Decision layers / 4. Navigation / 5. Archetype catalogue / 6. Group behaviors / 7. Performance budgets / 8. Debug & tuning hooks / 9. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- AI_Systems vs Enemy: *how it computes* here; *why it exists* in Enemy.
- Archetype IDs are referenced by Enemy/Encounter, never re-described.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every archetype declares its decision layer and perception inputs.
- Tuning parameters have ranges and owners.
